  "description": [
   {
    "value": "Mark Twain was the penname of American writer Samuel L. Clemens. He wrote numerous novels and short stories, some of which include science fictional or fantastic elements, including the time travel novel A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court (1889), \"The Undying Head\" (1883), and \"Extract from Captain Stormfield's Visit to Heaven\" (1907). Steven H Silver has argued that his novel Pudd'nhead Wilson can also be considered science fiction...",
    "lang": "en",
    "via": "llm-page:bio paragraph",
    "file": "P9307.json",
    "uri": false
